class:: Cx
summary:: External MIDI controller to Px pattern parameter bridge
categories:: Live Coding, MIDI
related:: Classes/Px, Classes/Dx, Classes/MIDIFunc

description::
Cx (Controller X) maps external MIDI controllers to Px pattern parameters. Rotary encoders, sliders, and buttons on a hardware controller can adjust parameters on active patterns without typing.

Mappings are declared in YAML files under code::Presets/cx/::. Each control (identified by CC number) targets one parameter (e.g. code::\amp::, code::\dur::) on the pattern occupying a given slot. Slot ordering mirrors the pattern GUI: drum-machine patterns first (alphabetical), then numeric ids ascending. Adding or removing patterns automatically shifts what each encoder targets.

The default mapping code::midilab3.yaml:: targets the 8 rotary encoders on an Arturia Midilab 3 (encoder mode set to Relative 1 = 2's complement).

subsection:: Basic Usage

code::
// Start some patterns
1 i: \sine dur: 1;
2 i: \saw dur: 0.5;
808 i: \bd dur: 1;

// Turn the controller on
Cx.play(\midilab3);

// See which encoder controls what
Cx.list;

// Debug incoming MIDI
Cx.debug = true;

// Stop listening (patterns keep playing)
Cx.stop;
::

subsection:: Config File Format

Each controller has its own YAML file. See code::Presets/cx/midilab3.yaml:: for the reference implementation.

code::
device: "Midilab 3"           # MIDIClient source name (nil = any source)
encoderMode: 2s_comp          # 2s_comp | signed_bit | bin_offset | absolute
controls:
  - cc: 74
    param: amp
    delta: 0.1                # step size per encoder tick
    min: 0.0
    max: 1.0
    default: 0.5              # used when target pattern has no value yet
    mode: signed_bit          # optional: override encoderMode for this control
    patternId: bd707          # optional: pin this slot to a specific id
::

Slot number = position in the code::controls:: list. Encoder in slot N targets the Nth pattern in code::Px.prSortedPatternIds:: unless a code::patternId:: is pinned in the row or via code::Cx.assign(slot, id)::.

subsection:: Encoder Modes

Relative encoders emit direction-only values. Configure the controller (e.g. via Arturia MIDI Control Center) to one of:

table::
## code::2s_comp:: || CW = 1..64, CCW = 127..65 (Arturia "Relative 1"). Recommended.
## code::signed_bit:: || CW = 65..127, CCW = 1..63 (Arturia "Relative 2").
## code::bin_offset:: || CW = 65..127, CCW = 63..0 (Arturia "Relative 3").
## code::absolute:: || Raw 0..127 mapped linearly to [min, max]. Use for sliders / real pots.
::

ClassMethods::

method:: play
Load a config (if not already loaded), open MIDI input, and register handlers. Idempotent — frees existing handlers first.

argument:: name
Symbol of the config file (without extension). Defaults to code::\midilab3:: on first call.

method:: stop
Free all MIDI handlers. Keeps the loaded config so code::Cx.play:: with no argument resumes.

method:: clear
Stop and drop the config and any pinned assignments.

method:: load
Load a YAML config without opening MIDI. Useful for inspecting a mapping before playing.

argument:: name
Symbol of the config file (without extension) in code::Presets/cx/::.

method:: list
Print the current slot → pattern id → param mapping.

method:: assign
Pin a slot to a specific pattern id, overriding the sorted-slot default.

argument:: slot
Integer slot number (1-based).

argument:: patternId
Symbol pattern id (e.g. code::\bd707::, code::\1::).

method:: debug
When code::true::, prints each incoming MIDI message with decoded step and target. Useful for verifying CC numbers and encoder mode.

Examples::

code::
// Set up a controller with mixed drum + synth patterns
1 i: \sine dur: 1;
2 i: \saw dur: 0.5;
808 i: \bd dur: 1;
808 i: \sd dur: 1;

Cx.play(\midilab3);
Cx.list;    // slot 1 → \bd808  amp, slot 2 → \sd808 amp, slot 3 → \1 amp, slot 4 → \2 amp ...

// Pin slot 1 to a specific pattern regardless of sort order
Cx.assign(1, \sd808);

// Reload a config after editing the YAML
Cx.load(\midilab3);
::
